iamentarians (Long Parliament)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War","c":2},{"y":1648,"t":"contest_end","x":"1648: Preston.","m":8,"cp":"Parliamentarians (Long Parliament)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War","c":3},{"y":1649,"t":"merge","x":"1649: the Commonwealth.","m":5,"cp":"commonwealth-of-england","cpn":"Commonwealth of England","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_England","c":3},{"y":1649,"t":"vassal_end","x":"19 May 1649: the Commonwealth.","m":5,"cp":"kingdom-of-ireland","cpn":"Kingdom of Ireland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Ireland","c":2},{"y":1660,"t":"gain","x":"1660: the Restoration.","m":5,"cp":"commonwealth-of-england","cpn":"Commonwealth of England","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_English_monarchs","c":3},{"y":1660,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1660: the Restoration.","m":5,"cp":"kingdom-of-ireland","cpn":"Kingdom of Ireland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Ireland","c":2},{"y":1660,"t":"rename","x":"1660: the Stuart restoration.","m":5,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_English_monarchs","c":3},{"y":1707,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1 May 1707: the Acts of Union.","m":5,"cp":"kingdom-of-ireland","cpn":"Kingdom of Ireland","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Ireland","c":2},{"y":1707,"t":"dissolve","x":"1707: England and Scotland unite as Great Britain.","m":5,"cp":"kingdom-of-great-britain","cpn":"Kingdom of Great Britain","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_England","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Æthelstan's invasion of Scotland","from":934,"to":934,"outcome":"No territorial result: Æthelstan set out in May 934, reached Chester-le-Street by late June or early July, and by September Constantine witnessed a charter at Buckingham as 'subregulus'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86thelstan"},{"name":"Battle of Brunanburh","from":937,"to":937,"outcome":"English victory: in 937 the Vikings and Scots invaded England and 'Æthelstan defeated them at the Battle of Brunanburh'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86thelstan"},{"name":"Eadred's reconquest of Northumbria","from":947,"to":954,"outcome":"English victory: the York magnates swore at Tanshelf (947), took Erik, then Anlaf, then Erik again (952); 'In 954, the York magnates again threw out Erik and returned to English rule' and Osulf was made 'ealdorman of the whole of Northumbria'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eadred"},{"name":"Danish conquest of England (Sweyn and Cnut)","from":1013,"to":1016,"outcome":"Danish victory: Sweyn conquers England in 1013 and dies on 3 February 1014; Cnut returns in September 1015, wins Assandun on 18 October 1016, takes the lands north of the Thames in the partition and, after Edmund Ironside's death on 30 November, 'all of…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cnut_the_Great"},{"name":"Norman Conquest","from":1066,"to":1071,"outcome":"Norman victory: Hardrada is beaten at Stamford Bridge on 25 September 1066; William lands at Pevensey on 28 September, wins Hastings on 14 October and is crowned on 25 December; resistance at Exeter (1068), in the north (the Harrying of the North, winter…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Conquest"},{"name":"First Barons' War","from":1216,"to":1217,"outcome":"English victory: Louis lands in Kent in May 1216, holds London and 'a third of England' by July, is beaten at Lincoln (20 May 1217) and at sea off Sandwich (24 August 1217) and leaves under the Treaty of Lambeth (11 September 1217).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Barons%27_War"},{"name":"Conquest of Wales by Edward I","from":1277,"to":1284,"outcome":"English victory: Aberconwy (November 1277): Llywelyn is 'left only with the western part of Gwynedd'; Llywelyn is killed on 11 December 1282, Dafydd captured in June 1283; the Statute of Rhuddlan (1284) annexes the royal lands to the crown, in six shires.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquest_of_Wales_by_Edward_I"},{"name":"First War of Scottish Independence","from":1296,"to":1328,"outcome":"Scottish victory: England rules Scotland from July 1296, loses it after Stirling Bridge (11 September 1297), regains it by the February 1304 submission, and loses it for good after Bannockburn (1314); the Treaty of Edinburgh-Northampton (1 May 1328)…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_War_of_Scottish_Independence"},{"name":"Hundred Years' War","from":1337,"to":1453,"outcome":"French victory: Calais taken in 1347; the Treaty of Brétigny (8 May 1360) gives 'increased lands in Aquitaine'; war resumes in 1369 and 'by the time Charles V died in 1380, the English held only Calais and a few other ports'; Henry V retakes Normandy (Caen…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hundred_Years%27_War"},{"name":"Desmond Rebellions","from":1569,"to":1583,"outcome":"English victory: 'the Earl of Desmond was killed in 1583'; the Desmond estates are forfeited (Desmond dossier) and the page puts the Munster plantation 'in the 1590s'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tudor_conquest_of_Ireland"},{"name":"Nine Years' War (Ireland)","from":1593,"to":1603,"outcome":"English victory: 'O'Neill openly broke with the crown in February 1595'; Spanish aid in 1596; Kinsale (1601); Mellifont signed 'mere days after the death of Elizabeth I' (24 March 1603): 'by 1603 the entire country was under English rule'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tudor_conquest_of_Ireland"},{"name":"Bishops' Wars","from":1639,"to":1640,"outcome":"Scottish success: in August 1640 a Scots army 'won a battle at Newburn and occupied parts of the north of England'; Charles agreed to pay the Scottish army's expenses (Ripon).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War"},{"name":"Irish Rebellion of 1641","from":1641,"to":1649,"outcome":"Confederate success until 1649: 'most of the island controlled by the Irish Confederates'; the war passes to the Commonwealth in 1649.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War"},{"name":"English Civil War","from":1642,"to":1651,"outcome":"Parliamentary victory: the king raised his standard on 22 August 1642; Naseby (14 June 1645); the king surrenders to the Scots in May 1646; the Second Civil War ends at Preston (17-19 August 1648); Charles I is beheaded on 30 January 1649; the Commonwealth is…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Civil_War"}],"certainty":[{"from":927,"to":1065,"level":"soft","note":"Anglo-Saxon and Danish frontiers are approximate: the Scottish march (Lothian to 973), the Welsh border (the Wye, 'fixed' at Hereford on the Æthelstan page, undated) and the Cornish boundary at the Tamar are not surveyed."},{"from":1066,"to":1534,"level":"soft","note":"The Welsh March, the Lordship of Ireland (the Pale's edge, Gaelic lordships), the Scottish border before 1328 and the Gascon frontier (Treaty of Brétigny, 8 May 1360, does not list the lands on the page) are soft; Calais (the Pale of…"},{"from":1535,"to":1602,"level":"sharp","note":"England and Wales are sharp after the Laws in Wales Acts (1535-1542) and the Statute of Rhuddlan shires; the Irish frontier is soft until 1603 ('by 1603 the entire country was under English rule')."},{"from":1603,"to":1707,"level":"sharp","note":"England, Wales and the shired parts of Ireland are sharp; the Scottish border is the Union of the Crowns' border between two kingdoms (the Debatable Lands were divided in 1552, Scotland dossier)."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_England","title":"Kingdom of England"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86thelstan","title":"Æthelstan"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eadred","title":"Eadred"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cnut_the_Great","title":"Cnut the Great"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Conquest","title":"Norman Conquest"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lordship_of_Ireland","title":"Lordship of Ireland"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Barons%27_War","title":"First Barons' War"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi